I have a problem with the way that  Oxford advertises itself to students  because while the University and the  colleges and the departments have saw  the best websites of any educational  institution about a scene it's all facts  there's no feeling behind it you don't  ever get the feeling of what it's like  to be a student at Oxford it's a very  top-down approach this institution which  kind of preaches to you gives you all  this information what I want to try and  do is a bottom-up approach so rather  than an institution preaching to you and  giving you all these facts and figures I  want to show you the view from the  ground boots on the ground view of being  a student so from one student to an  applicant what it's like to be a student  at Oxford and the way I want to dig well  we want to try and do that is making a  vlog every week with what I've been  doing in my work what are we doing  outside of my work how I've been  socializing the kind of events that are  going on in Oxford just to give you the  experience to give you the feeling  rather than the fact I figured is  nothing else that is an interesting  experiment just to see if this will take  off as a form of access  so what I've been doing this week is not  very much  this is freshers week in Oxford so um  Sunday all the freshers come up move  into their rooms and a lot of second  years and third years and in my case for  theatres come back help people with  moving in help them settle in and make  the most of being in Oxford but not  having to do lots and lots of work  already so I'm a fourth year student  which means that I'm technically part of  the JCR junior common room for  undergraduates but also the MCR middle :  room for graduate students because  technically I am a graduate student I  haven't graduated yet it's a bit weird  so freshers week for me is a bit strange  because I'm invited to all the MCR  events but I go to all the JCR events  and in a way I'm almost expected to go  to some of the JCR events and to be  honest I do myself as being much more  part of the junior corner in the middle  column just because that's what my  friends are so I've been mostly going to  JCR event so the kind of thing that  they've been doing is they have a big  marquee in little college one of the  quads and there's a bar Bothell bar in  there where we've been doing some  drinking games some Gangnam style  dancing though the club lights  Sun lights though I really should point  out there's no pressure whatsoever to go  to them when I was in my freshers week  in first year I went I think one club  night I'm just not a clubbing type  person I thought I'd give it a go this  time round so there was a phone party  yet Junction never been to a phone party  before and it was an experience I'll say  that I was right in front of a cannon  source just being like blasted with foam  but part of that it's apart from the  organised events for the JCR a lot of  what goes on this week is just kind of  reacquainting yourself with Oxford so  you're not doing work yet but you have  the time so so you have the time to  wander around the city to you know  reacquaint yourself with all the places  that you missed out on if the Sun  doesn't set I have been doing any work  this year  I am for Thea physicist and I get to  choose two major options for what I want  to do as effectively for my master's  year so I'm choosing to do theoretical  physics and atmospheric Oceanic and  planetary physics which are two kind of  opposite ends of the spectrum because  the full list of options is God  astrophysics  atmospheric Oceanic and Planetary  biological physics condensed matter  physics quantum information processing  in lasers particle physics and  theoretical physics  so theoretical physics is the most  mathematical whereas atmospheric physics  is I'll give you the closest thing to  something like geography so it's not as  maths heaviness more than a physical  understanding required and I'm like both  of those aspects admittedly I'm much  better the physical and standing stuff  because I wasn't doing physics i viddied  geography so the theoretical option is  something that I'm almost doing as a  test to myself to make myself get better  at maths because I want to apply to do a  DPhil PhD in atmospheric physics but I  want to do the more mathematical side of  things I'm interested in global climate  processes which was what I did in my  work over the summer so I've been doing  preliminary reading for both of those  courses and cracking on with the  vacation work so there's a there's a  problem set for each of them what's as  problems there for one there's a few  questions for the theoretical option  which i've been doing i've also been  preparing for my conference talk because  on sunday i am going to germany to  present the paper that I wrote over the  summer with my supervisor Scott Osprey  about the face synchronization of the  quasi vinyl and a semi animal  oscillation and again that's in the  video I made but I'm off to Germany to  present this paper at an international  conference which is just phenomenal I  really wasn't expecting to have the  opportunity to do that but it's a  fantastic boost of the CV you know  revealing to do this work over the  summer was a privilege but being able to  present a paper but publish a paper  about it and present my paper a  conference it's just such an incredible  boost to my academic cv I'm really  really lucky to be able to do it see ya  this works been quite different from  most other weeks and I've had every  other week in the  apart from the the week after you  finished your exams so in future weeks  what I'm gonna be talking about is the  kind the amount of work that I've been  doing without going into too much than  itty-bitty detail some of the content  I'm going to be doing but also stuff  outside of it so this term I'm taking a  lot stuff outside of my subjects so I'm  doing a meditation course that the  mindfulness Center here in Oxford we  have got a guy called professor Marc  Williams who's like a world leader in  the field of mindfulness meditation so I  thought good opportunity take a take him  up on it I'm also now on the committee  for the university physics society and  that's something I am you talking about  a lot in the future probably but we have  a talk to next week about nuclear fusion  which I will report back on and the  social actually physics and socials  don't only go together but sometimes we  need sign to have a center bring but  also the big thing that I'm going to be  doing this term is the College YouTube  channel as I have probably mentioned in  the past I may be each hotel my college  and it was the first student made  college YouTube channel in Oxford and we  focused previously on aspects of the  college like accommodation sport music  that kind of thing what is this time  we're going to be doing it a  half-a-dozen subject specific videos so  there's five or six minute videos about  history say and the kind of stuff that  they're looking for in applicants the  nature of the course meeting with the  tutors getting them to describe their  work and talking to students about their  experiences of the course so that's  going to be a big part of my term in  addition to the really quite  considerable amount of work I'm going to  be doing basically I want this to useful  to people I'm not just doing this as  like a self-indulgent thing I want to  help anybody who's applying give even  they have to give them the idea what  it's like to be here so if you have a  question that you'd like me to answer or  if you have something you'd like me to  cover in a video I really really like to  hear from you so you know leave a  comment on this video give me a message  and I'll do my best to incorporate that  what I'll probably do is not on to  comment on the video in the comment  section I've already revised a comment  in the subsequent video so yeah you'll  be hearing from me in a week's time  when I come back from Germany and I have  started the course proper and we've had  our first physics society event and  terms got going anyway I hope this is  going to be useful and I will see you  next week

